        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 02-964, George Baldwin v. Michael Reese."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gen. Hardy Myers (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MYERS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: When a state prisoner decides to attack his conviction on the basis of a claimed violation of Federal constitutional right, your cases have held that he must first alert the state courts he is raising a Federal claim, if that claim is to be exhausted for Federal habeas purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, we're reviewing a Ninth Circuit holding, which seems fairly open-ended. How would you characterize the Ninth Circuit rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: How about if you cite at least a - a reported case that has decided the claim on a Federal basis? You make your claim and cite a case that -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Don't you think it's likely that Federal judges sitting in the state would be aware of those changes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Record",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the papers that were submitted to the court of appeals did not advise or tell that court that a Federal question was being raised, a Federal claim was being raised."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Balske",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have a narrow question of fair presentation here, and it isn't a great effort for the courts, I don't believe, in Mr. Reese's case, to go searching to find that he did fairly present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Oregon Statute",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's 138.640. It's at the state's brief in the appendix at page 4, and it reads as follows, quote, the order making final disposition of the petition shall state clearly the grounds upon which the cause was determined, and whether a state or Federal question, or both, was presented and decided."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Balske",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do not defend the Ninth Circuit's test. I only defend the judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Record",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "sustain their judgment was to adopt this rule of - that the appellate court has the duty, or is presumed to have understood what happened in the trial court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But we get thousands of cases around here that just says Fifth Amendment, ineffective assistance of counsel. That gives us very, very little help."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the purpose of the exhaustion rule is to give him a fair opportunity to decide it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "section 11 of the Oregon constitution, quote, Oregon courts often refer to inadequate assistance of counsel instead of ineffective assistance of counsel, the term usually employed by the state and Federal courts in applying the analogous provision of the Federal Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, if you - you say that the Ninth Circuit approach to this was wrong, which - which seems to be anchored in, if it's clear that the court of first instance relied on the Federal ground, that stays with the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: If you prevail, I hope you're not unhappy with what you get, because you're going to have petitions in which there's a huge laundry list of cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MYERS",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MYERS: Your Honor, indeed, the fact that Federal - or that the Federal source of the claim is used is not the end of the fair presentation issue, because there's still going to be the ongoing requirement of adequately identifying your substance of your claim, to use the terminology of this Court, the - the legal theory as well as the adequacy of the fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-964",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9fb568e8dd21498dae6949d96e5f22b346a51cf2c040d30a1f1615b76a5cccd6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9fb568e8dd21-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, General Myers. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
